        <briefdescription>
<para>Runs a self-test on the driver and device. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The test:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Resets the device,</para></listitem><listitem><para>Writes a value into the Alarm Threshold register and reads it back for comparison.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Resets the device again.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_sys_mon_psu" kindref="compound">XSysMonPsu</ref> instance.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS if the value read from the Alarm Threshold register is the same as the value written.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE Otherwise.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>This is a destructive test in that resets of the device are performed. Refer to the device specification for the device status after the reset operation. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
